# Temporary working files
scratchpad-*.txt

# Composer/editor save-backups written next to book/ artifacts (.md.bak, .json.bak)
content/**/*.bak

# Backup / editor-swap / conflict artifacts — repo-wide preventive hardening
*.bak
*.old
*.orig
*~

# site-health-sentinel throwaway screenshots (created + deleted per QA run)
plan-dashboard/.visual-qa/

# OS files
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Claude Code (per-machine local state)
.claude/

# Editor files
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.code-workspace

# Stray scratch dirs (large binary outputs — m4a is audio rendering)
/m4a/
/content/m4a/
/CONTENT/m4a/

# Python virtual environment
.venv/

# Python bytecode caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Test runner caches (regenerated on each run)
.pytest_cache/
.benchmarks/

# STALE/RETIRED: there is no separate podcast-reader app — the reader is a
# section inside the Podcast Factory Astro Site (plan-dashboard/). This ignore
# entry is retired and harmless (no such directory); kept only for safety.
podcast-reader/

# Node / server proxy
server/node_modules/
server/.logs/
server/logs/*.jsonl
server/data/*.db
server/data/*.db-wal
server/data/*.db-shm
server/data/backups/
node_modules/

# Astro generated content-collection types (regenerated by `astro dev`).
.astro/
**/.astro/

# Environment files (API keys should live in macOS Keychain, not .env)
.env
.env.local
*.env
!*.template.env
# infra/azure/azure-config.env is intentionally tracked: it holds resource
# names + the subscription ID (publicly visible in any portal URL), no
# secrets. Tracking it lets a new Mac `git clone && make bootstrap` without
# manually copying the template. (Real secrets live in macOS Keychain via
# store-keychain-keys.sh or Azure Key Vault.)
!infra/azure/azure-config.env

# _workspace/ is the tracked execution-plan + per-book authoring zone.
# .DS_Store inside it is still excluded by the OS-junk rule above.
# (Historical: a `_workspace/Books/` capital-B PDF drop-zone was once planned
# but never materialized; the gitignore line was retired 2026-05-23 because
# it silently collided with `_workspace/books/` on case-insensitive macOS,
# eating new per-book files. PDFs live at the parent `raw/` per intake_book.py.)

# Podcast raw-input binaries (audio, video, archives, editing-project files)
# — large assets that live under _workspace/<category>/<slug>/_source/. Only
# derived text artifacts (refined chapters, episode txts, kept transcripts)
# get committed. Keeps the repo small regardless of where binaries land.
# Post-Phase-9.5: workspace lives at root-level _workspace/ (not content/podcast/library/).
_workspace/**/*.mp3
_workspace/**/*.wav
_workspace/**/*.m4a
_workspace/**/*.mp4
_workspace/**/*.mov

# Post-2026-05-23 restructure: per-book audio dumps live under
# content/drafts/<slug>/mp3/ (NotebookLM downloads that we Azure-transcribe).
# Same policy as _workspace audio above — keep the repo small.
content/drafts/**/mp3/
content/drafts/**/*.mp3
content/drafts/**/*.wav
content/drafts/**/*.m4a
content/drafts/**/*.mp4
content/drafts/**/*.mov

# Post-2026-06-04 type-first layout: content lives at content/<Bucket>/<slug>/.
# Per-book audio (raw input + NotebookLM renders) stays OUT of git at ANY bucket
# path — same small-repo policy as above. (The old content/drafts/** rules are
# kept for history/back-compat.)
# (`/**` + .gitkeep negation, not bare dir rules: a dir-level exclude would
#  also swallow the skeleton's .gitkeep markers — see _paths.ensure_book_skeleton)
content/**/mp3/**
content/**/m4a/**
!content/**/mp3/.gitkeep
!content/**/m4a/.gitkeep
content/**/*.mp3
content/**/*.wav
content/**/*.m4a
content/**/*.mp4
content/**/*.mov
content/**/*.llc
# Per-book scratch — transcription probes, rejected drafts, scratchpads. Never
# committed; the orchestrator pre-flight treats untracked files as a dirty tree.
content/**/_system/scratchpad/

# Studio editor in-progress drafts (unapproved edits). Promoted to chapters/<id>.txt
# on approval, then deleted; never committed — half-finished edits stay local.
content/**/_system/drafts/
CONTENT/**/_system/drafts/
_workspace/**/*.zip
_workspace/**/*.llc
_workspace/**/*.pdf

# PDF policy (locked 2026-06-09):
# - SOURCE PDFs are intentionally TRACKED — irreplaceable pipeline inputs,
#   written once (content/<Bucket>/<slug>/_source/ and _system/source/).
#   Git doubles as their backup; do not add ignore rules for them.
# - GENERATED reading-edition PDFs under book/ are IGNORED — derived from
#   book.md via build_book_pdf.py, regenerable at any time, delivered to
#   Google Drive from disk. Tracking them would grow git history by megabytes
#   on every re-render.
content/**/book/*.pdf
# - Studio Preview's per-page PNG cache is IGNORED — derived from book.pdf by
#   plan-dashboard/scripts/lib/preview-pages.mjs (pdftoppm), regenerated
#   whenever the PDF changes.
content/**/book/_preview-cache/
# - Extracted slide-deck page rasters are IGNORED — derived from the tracked
#   deck PDFs by inject_slide_deck.py/_slide_import.py (pdftoppm), regenerable.
#   The deck PDFs + PPTX themselves stay tracked as source-of-truth inputs;
#   _manifests/*.json (slide→anchor maps) are tracked, their .sig caches not.
content/**/slide-decks/_pages/
content/**/slide-decks/_manifests/.*-sig
# - Slide OCR/vision analysis JSONs are TRACKED (expensive per-chapter AI pass,
#   cached across sessions); only the .sig cache-invalidation files are ignored.
content/**/slide-decks/_analysis/.*-sig

# Transcript working artifacts — raw Speech-to-Text + translator output used
# during chapter-source authoring. The final cleaned chapters/ + episodes/
# files are committed; transcripts/ is local-only scratch.
_workspace/lectures/*/transcripts/

# Sandbox inbox — universal drop zone for raw inputs (MP3, PDF, TurboScribe
# txt, etc.) before the podcast agent triages them into the right book dir.
# Nothing inside should ever be committed; only the README documents the
# contract. See _workspace/_sandbox/README.md.
_workspace/_sandbox/*
!_workspace/_sandbox/README.md

# Phase 9.5 — per-book workspace at _workspace/books/<slug>/
# Track orchestrator state + chapters + episode drafts; ignore raw source intake.
# On case-insensitive macOS APFS, _workspace/Books/ (capital B) and _workspace/books/
# resolve to the same directory; we list both for case-sensitive filesystems too.
_workspace/books/*/source*
_workspace/books/*/*.pdf
_workspace/books/*/raw/
_workspace/Books/*/source*
_workspace/Books/*/*.pdf
_workspace/Books/*/raw/

# inbox — large-file drop zone for raw inputs pending triage/filing.
# Nothing inside should ever be committed.
_workspace/inbox/*
!_workspace/inbox/.gitkeep

# wave-chain-auth.json — operator pre-authorization envelope written at runtime.
# Contains spend caps + authorized wave list; not source code; not committed.
_workspace/plan/operations/wave-chain-auth.json

# KAHSKOLE / KSESSIONS extraction work zone (added 2026-05-24).
# Scripts + extracted output are tracked; exclude the ~750MB source SQL
# dumps (backed up in Google Drive — re-importable as needed).
_workspace/kashkole-ksessions/*.sql
# source-library: exclude the SQL dumps AND the built SQLite corpora (e.g.
# wisdom-corpus.db, ~11MB) — large binaries, re-buildable from the dumps.
# (case fixed 2026-06-08: was uppercase CONTENT/, silently broken on
#  case-sensitive filesystems.)
content/_shared/source-library/*.sql
content/_shared/source-library/*.db
content/_shared/source-library/*.db-shm
content/_shared/source-library/*.db-wal
content/knowledge-base/*.db
!content/knowledge-base/mirror.db
content/knowledge-base/*.db-shm
content/knowledge-base/*.db-wal

# Astro site dev-time SQLite mirror — generated locally, never committed.
plan-dashboard/knowledge.db
plan-dashboard/knowledge.db-shm
plan-dashboard/knowledge.db-wal

# Dev-server daemon logs (launchd, pm2, etc.) — regenerated on every start.
plan-dashboard/dev.launchd*.log
plan-dashboard/*.launchd*.log

# Wave L categorization run artifacts — reproducible via categorize_atoms.py;
# the committed knowledge.db carries the source-of-truth content_level values.
# (Both case variants listed for the macOS APFS / git case-fold mismatch.)
content/knowledge-base/categorize-report.json
content/knowledge-base/categorize-review.json
CONTENT/knowledge-base/categorize-report.json
CONTENT/knowledge-base/categorize-review.json

# Auto-generated pipeline metrics — reproducible from the DB, never committed.
# (Both case variants for macOS APFS / git case-fold mismatch.)
content/drafts/**/_system/stage-metrics.json
CONTENT/drafts/**/_system/stage-metrics.json
# Post-2026-06-04 type-first layout: the Studio reader rewrites stage-metrics.json
# on every load and the cost summary writes cost-validation.json — derived, never
# source-of-truth, must not dirty the tree at ANY bucket path.
content/**/_system/stage-metrics.json
content/**/_system/cost-validation.json

# Root-level package-lock.json (belongs only in plan-dashboard/; the root
# package.json is metadata-only with no install dependencies).
/package-lock.json

# Pre-augmentation backups written by the augmenter before it rewrites episode
# files — transient safety copies, never committed.
**/.before-augment/

# Python bytecode
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Trash / soft-delete staging
**/.trash/

# Per-trip queue + ephemeral artifacts (App writes, Cowork drains and deletes per §5.10)
trips/*/pending.json
trips/*/receipts/
trips/*/photos/
trips/*/voice-inbox/
trips/*/voice-inbox.json
trips/*/itinerary-inbox.json
trips/*/snapshots/


# Wrangler local cache (regenerated per invocation)
.wrangler/
_workspace/orchestrator-logs/
_workspace/scratch/
_workspace/tmp/
# Local-only audio/voice experiment sandbox (ElevenLabs auditions, prototype
# scripts). Never a branch deliverable — keep on disk, out of git.
_workspace/experiments/

# Per-session chat scratch notes — now tracked for cross-Mac handoff
# (was local-only until 2026-05-19; tracked thereafter per user directive).
# Add any sensitive/per-machine subdirectories explicitly here if needed.

# Chunked-window scratch (orchestrator runtime artifacts — regenerable from
# raw-extract.md). Broader **/_chunks/ catches any future caller that writes
# _chunks/ outside the canonical book directory.
**/_chunks/

# Local-only orchestrator/runtime logs and supervisor run registry
_workspace/logs/
_workspace/runs/

# Local-only audit snapshots (pre-rerun copies of book artifacts for diff/review)
_workspace/audit/

# Local-only experiment scratch (audio smoke-tests, voice auditions, one-off
# spikes) — kept on disk but never tracked; not source-of-truth for any pipeline.
_workspace/experiments/

# Sanitizer backups (created by scripts/podcast/sanitize_contract_yaml.py)
*.yml.bak

# Studio find-and-replace one-step backups (created by /api/studio/replace)
*.txt.bak

# Framing signature cache (runtime hash used by pipeline to detect framing changes)
.framing-sig

# VSCode workspace favorites (user-local IDE state)
.favorites.json
raw/
.cache/

# Stale legacy content/drafts/ stub (retired 2026-06-04 type-first migration)
content/drafts/

# Generated video-layer images — Imagen3 backgrounds + Pillow-rendered teaching slides.
# Regenerable from video-prompts.json via generate_video_layer.py; not source-of-truth.
content/**/video-images/
# Watchdog sentinel files — ephemeral PID/state files written/deleted per run;
# never source-of-truth, must not dirty the tree between orchestrator invocations.
content/**/_system/watchdog.json

# Source archives (TurboScribe exports, zip dumps) — large binaries kept on disk
# but not tracked in git; re-exportable from TurboScribe or Google Drive.
content/**/*.zip

# Orchestrator run logs in the review archive — were accidentally committed
# during kitab-al-riyad development; future logs stay untracked.
_workspace/reviews/archive/**/*.log
_workspace/reviews/logs/*.log
# temp YNAB files
_workspace/ynab-*

# transient per-run orchestrator/allocator logs in content dirs
content/**/run-*.log
content/**/_alloc/run.log
content/**/_system/_synthesis-run.log
